  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q57-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "57",
    "prompt": "Given the coefficient of $x$ is $0$ in the expansion of $(1+ax)^4(1-4x)^3$, find the coefficient of $x^2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-42$",
      "worked": "The coefficient of $x$ is $4a-12$. Thus\n$$\\begin{align*}4a-12&=0\\\\a&=3.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x^2$, match powers $2+0$, $1+1$ and $0+2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Coefficient of }x^2&=\\binom{4}{2}a^2+(4a)(-12)+\\binom{3}{2}(-4)^2\\\\\\text{Coefficient of }x^2&=6a^2-48a+48\\\\\\text{Coefficient of }x^2&=6(3)^2-48(3)+48\\\\\\text{Coefficient of }x^2&=-42.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 68
  },
